# Configure the CEC adapter (physical address from EDID + logical address as
# a playback device) as soon as the kernel creates /dev/cec0. Without this,
# the adapter has no logical/physical address and joystick-notify's CEC
# wake/active-source/set-stream-path calls have nothing valid to send from.
# See https://wiki.archlinux.org/title/HDMI-CEC
#
# Generalized from v1: no connector name is hardcoded here — jn-cec0-configure
# (src/joystick_notify/cec0_configure.py) reads the couch output port from
# config.toml at runtime instead.
#
# No ACTION=="add" match: the systemd tag must be re-applied on every event,
# or a "change" event drops it, systemd deactivates dev-cec0.device, and
# cec0-configure.service (BindsTo=dev-cec0.device) stops for good. Arch's
# udev-reload pacman hook runs `udevadm trigger -c change` after any package
# touching udev rules (including this one), which left the adapter
# unconfigured (phys f.f.f.f, no logical address) on 2026-10-23. systemd only
# acts on SYSTEMD_WANTS when the device unit becomes active, so this does not
# restart the service on every change event.
SUBSYSTEM=="cec", KERNEL=="cec0", TAG+="systemd", ENV{SYSTEMD_WANTS}="cec0-configure.service"
